900 C1$="David spoke.":C2$="Susanna spoke.":C3$="The Devil King spoke.":C4$="The King of the North spoke."
1000 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6100:BM$="David ran down the hallway.":GOSUB 5100
1010 BM$="He kept running, trying to reach the wall he could see ahead... However, he\was not getting any closer to it, as if he were simply stomping his feet on\the spot.":GOSUB 5100
1020 GOSUB 6110:BM$="He was getting tired. He stopped running and looked back. Nobody was\chasing him.":GOSUB 5100
1025 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 6120:BM$="He made his way back, and stopped, dumbfounded.":GOSUB 5100
1030 BM$="The wall he had been trying so hard to reach was right in front of him.\There was a door in it.":GOSUB 5100
1040 GOSUB 9505:GOSUB 6130:BM$="David pushed the door without hesitation. With a creaking noise, it opened.":GOSUB 5100
1050 POLL X:GOSUB 6140:BM$="When he saw the room, he was left speechless.":GOSUB 5100
1060 BM$="It was the same room he had been sleeping in. Every item, every piece of\furniture was in the same place. Even his own luggage was there.":GOSUB 5100
1070 BM$="As if sleepwalking, he made his way inside.":GOSUB 5100
1080 BM$="`When I left the room, Susanna didn't chase me,` David thought. `Maybe I'm\under the effects of a hypnotic spell...`":GOSUB 5100
1090 COMMON FO:BM$="`I ran so much, but I'm back where I started...`":GOSUB 5100
1095 GOSUB 9010:'
1100 GOSUB 6150:BM$="David felt a presence, and turned towards the entrance. It was dark\outside the room, with only candles breaking the darkness.":GOSUB 5100
1110 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 6160:GOSUB 9545:GOSUB 6330:FOR I=0 TO 1000:NEXT:GOSUB 6330:BM$="Suddenly, a bolt of lightning lit up the corridor, a sound so loud that it felt\like the heavens themselves had split. Then, there was a figure in front of\the entrance.":GOSUB 5100
1120 BM$="David, I have come for you. Come with me to the basement, and witness the\blood of that man.":GOSUB 5100
1130 GOSUB 9545:GOSUB 6330:BM$="As the lightnings kept flashing, David was able to see the face of the man.\It was the other David, the one he met in the basement.":GOSUB 5100
1140 BM$="David: If... If you're the real David, why don't YOU go to the basement?! Why\do I have to go?!":GOSUB 5100
1150 BM$="Other David: Because there should not be two Davids. Only by witnessing\the blood of the northern tribes will we become one. If you will not do so,\then you must vanish!":GOSUB 5100
1160 GOSUB 6170:BM$="His other self approached him, brandishing a knife.":GOSUB 5100
1170 BM$="David tried to dodge the knife, but its aim was true. It pierced his heart.":GOSUB 5100
1180 BM$="David: AAAHHH!!":GOSUB 5100
1190 GOSUB 9526:BM$="David's scream echoed throughout the room.":GOSUB 5100
1195 POLL X:GOSUB 9030:GOSUB 9900:GOSUB 9550:GOSUB 9510:GOSUB 9530:'
1200 GOSUB 6140:BM$="Then, he opened his eyes.":GOSUB 5100
1210 BM$="`It was another nightmare,` David thought. `Is this reality? Or am I still\dreaming?`":GOSUB 5100
1220 BM$="He was losing his mind thinking about it. He decided to lie on the bed and\close his eyes, trying to calm down.":GOSUB 5100
1230 COMMON FO:GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 6190:GOSUB 9010:BM$="King of the North: You are trying to kill one of my tribesmen. My curse may\have failed, but now that I am here, I shall run my sword through your\heart!":GOSUB 5100:'
1240 BM$="The King of the North appeared in his room. He approached David,\brandishing his sword.":GOSUB 5100
1250 BM$="David stood up, looking for a chance to flee. When the King of the North\had lowered his guard, he made his move.":GOSUB 5100
1260 GOSUB 6180:BM$="But then, he heard King Hroth's voice inside his head.":GOSUB 5100
1270 BM$="King Hroth: You cannot defy fate, David! If you wish to defeat the King of\the North, you must witness the blood of the northern tribes! Without the\powers of the Devil King, the King of the North will kill you!":GOSUB 5100
1280 BM$="King Hroth: The one who stands before you is but a shadow. Focus your\eyes on the sword and he will not be able to kill you. Go to the basement!\Susanna is waiting for you! Hurry!":GOSUB 5100
1290 GOSUB 6200:BM$="The King of the North aimed his sword at David's chest. At the last moment,\he was able to dodge the strike, then he tackled his assailant.":GOSUB 5100
1300 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 6210:BM$="He had expected some kind of impact, but the King of the North must have\been an illusion. He passed through him, tumbling into the corridor.":GOSUB 5100
1310 GOSUB 9515:BM$="In a frenzy, he hurried down the stairs.":GOSUB 5100
1320 GOSUB 6220:BM$="Fearing that a sword could pierce his back at any moment, he kept running\down the corridor.":GOSUB 5100
1330 GOSUB 6230:ISET X:BM$="At the end, he turned right, and reached the door at the end, where he\stopped.":GOSUB 5100
1340 GOSUB 6240:BM$="`It's the door that leads to the basement,` David thought. `Did the Devil\King lead me here? No, I can't open it...`":GOSUB 5100
1350 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 6170:BM$="When he turned around, intent on going back, he saw a knife right before\his eyes.":GOSUB 5100
1360 BM$="Other David: You have come this far. Why turn back? You must go to the\basement, David! Do it, or I will kill you!":GOSUB 5100
1370 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6220:BM$="David shook off the knife, pushing his other self away, and ran away. He\could think of nothing else. He had to run.":GOSUB 5100
1380 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6310:ISET X:BM$="As he approached the dining room, he saw the King of the North, sword in\hand, coming down the stairs.":GOSUB 5100
1385 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6320:BM$="And so David ran. He ran. He kept running. He eventually reached the door\that led to the courtyard.":GOSUB 5100
1390 GOSUB 9535:GOSUB 5205:GOSUB 5615:BM$="He opened the door and jumped outside, without even stopping to look.":GOSUB 5100
